{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Not one day shall you eat, nor two days.</b> Double. <b>Nor five days</b> — corresponding to the fingers of the eating hand. <b>Nor ten days</b> — double for both his hands. <b>Nor twenty days</b> — in the manner of the expression, he will eat all that is eaten by the fingers of his hands and his feet. <b>Until a month of days</b> — until the circuit of the moon returns to its place as it was. <b>Until it comes out of your nostrils</b> — its meaning is until the smell goes out, for the sense of smell is in the nose. <b>And it shall be to you</b> — the meat of craving — <b>for loathing (לזרא)</b>: for the longing of desire will turn back to you as a great loathing, in the manner of what is written concerning Amnon's sister (II Samuel 13:15): ״כי גדולה השנאה אשר שנאה מאהבה אשר אהבה״ — for greater was the hatred with which he hated her than the love with which he loved her. And from this the word לזרא is written with an aleph, for the intensification of the loathing; for every word that should properly be written with a heh and is written with an aleph, the intent is to magnify the matter. And like it (Ruth 1:20): ״קראן לי מרא״ — which should have been with a heh, and its meaning is: do not call me Marah like every other bitter woman, but rather call me Marra, to intensify the bitterness, and this is ״כי המר שדי לי מאד״. And like it (Daniel 11:4): ״ויצא בחמא גדולה״ — where חמא is written with an aleph to magnify the wrath, which is why it says ״גדולה״. And so too here, the word לזרא is to magnify the loathing; this is what it says: ״until it comes out of your nostrils.״ And so it will happen to all who are drawn after the lusts of this world, who complain and weep over what their soul has not attained, and who disparage matters of the intellect and find fault with them — in the end the lusts will go out of their nostrils, until they descend to Sheol. And so Solomon, peace be upon him, likened the lusts of this world, which are sweet at first, to honeycomb; this is what he said (Proverbs 5:3): ״נופת תטופנה שפתי זרה וחלק משמן חכה״ — and he explained what will happen at its end, this is what he said: ״ואחריתה מרה כלענה חדה כחרב פיות״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:26.594815610Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}